        "original_id": "0f30b162-d166-580f-858b-2f7616c6c2f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Rhys-Davies, Timothy Dalton\n- Products: The Untouchables, Shōgun, Sliders, Robin of Sherwood, The Living Daylights, I, Claudius, James Bond film series\n- Roles: Agent Michael Malone, Pilot Vasco Rodrigues, Professor Maximillian Arturo, King Richard I, General Leonid Pushkin, Macro, James Bond\n\nFacts:\n- In 1987, The Living Daylights was released as the fifteenth film in the James Bond film series.\n- In 1987, Timothy Dalton became the first actor to star in The Living Daylights as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.\n- In The Living Daylights, John Rhys-Davies played General Leonid Pushkin.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Macro in I, Claudius.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the mini-series Shōgun.\n- John Rhys-Davies played King Richard I in Robin of Sherwood.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Professor Maximillian Arturo in Sliders.\n- In 1993, John Rhys-Davies played Agent Michael Malone in the remake of the 1950s television series The Untouchables.",
